# Root .gitignore for kanbantic-claude-plugin (KBT-B605).
#
# Until this file existed, the only .gitignore in the repo lived in plugin/ and
# covered plugin/ alone. `git add -A` at the root therefore picked up whatever
# agents had left lying around — including their git worktrees, which git
# silently records as embedded repositories. A clone of the outer repo then
# contains neither the content nor any way to fetch it. Git does warn, but the
# warning scrolls past in the output of an otherwise successful commit and
# blocks nothing.
#
# Observed at KBT-T4030 (PR #70), where two foreign worktrees made it into a
# commit and were only caught by a manual pre-push read-through.

# --- Agent worktrees -------------------------------------------------------
# Parallel agents create these; they are private to one agent and must never be
# committed. Three conventions are in use across the tooling.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `.claude/`: shared .claude/ content stays trackable,
# and a blanket rule would also change what the sync script sees when it checks
# gitignore coverage (KBT-B540). Only the worktree subdirectory is excluded.
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/
.wt-*/

# --- Dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
# package.json at the root drives the test harness, so node_modules/ can appear
# here as well as under plugin/.
node_modules/

# --- OS and editor cruft ---------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
